  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) Sec 1, 2-7-112(c)(1) (accepted ID: physical Tennessee driver licence)\n(quote) 2-7-112(c)(1), is amended by inserting the language \"physical\" immediately preceding the language \"Tennessee driver license\".\n(section) Sec 2, 2-7-112(c)(3)\n(quote) 2-7-112(c)(3), is amended by inserting the language \"physical,\" immediately after the language \"A\".\n(section) Sec 6, 55-50-306(e) (digital licence barred for voting)\n(quote) except, that to verify the person's identification for the purpose of voting, the person shall not present or submit evidence of possession of a valid driver license in a digital format, and a digital driver license must not be accepted as such evidence.\n(section) Sec 8, new 55-50-306(k) (the bar covers the free photo ID licence too)\n(quote) For purposes of this section, \"driver license\" includes a photo identification license issued under\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) Sec 3: 55-50-306 'electronic' becomes 'digital' (driver licence system wording).\n(other) Sec 4: 55-50-304 exemption for a person 18 or older doing a driving demonstration with a safety employee.\n(other) Sec 5: no fee to take part in the digital driver licence system.\n(other) Sec 7: data from a digital licence kept no more than 3 calendar days; not sold except to law enforcement, entitled governments or on subpoena.\n(other) Sec 8: biometric and geolocation limits; no required or preferred use of digital licence; digital licence disabled when the physical licence is cancelled, revoked or suspended or the device is lost or stolen.\n(other) Sec 9: 55-50-102(22)(D) Class D licence definition includes autocycles.\n(other) Sec 10: effective on becoming law.\n(other) version: 3106468-Draft (2025-02-06): carries slot a (Secs 1, 2, 6, 8(k)). Sec 6 says a digital licence 'must be accepted' for other identification but not for voting. Sec 8(g)(2)-(4): detailed biometric limits with consent each time and destruction within 3 days.\n(other) version: amend-239736-HA0118 (House Transportation amendment 1, Howell, dated 2025-03-19; action log says adopted on the House floor 2025-04-07 although the adopted flag reads 0): rewrites Sec 6 ('may be accepted' in place of 'must be accepted'; adds a comma before 'and a digital driver license') and Sec 8 (biometric limit shortened to the face-photo comparison; (h) adds 'including a photograph'). Voting-ID bar unchanged. Slot a unchanged.\n(other) version: 3223007-Chaptered (2025-04-25, Public Chapter 297, House Bill 1316 substituted for Senate Bill 1297): equals the Draft with HA0118's Sec 6 and Sec 8. Slot a carried.\n(other) note: Existing 2-7-112(c)(1) and (c)(3) list the accepted IDs (not reprinted here); the bill only inserts 'physical' before each. The bill's ID effect: a phone or other digital driver licence (and a digital photo ID licence) cannot be shown to vote; a physical licence still can. HA0118's adopted flag (0) conflicts with the action log ('H. adopted am. (Amendment 1 - HA0118)', 2025-04-07); the Chaptered text confirms the HA0118 wording became law. Senate amendment SA0055 was withdrawn 2025-04-10 (text not saved).",
